WEBVTT

00:00:00.240 --> 00:00:04.380
Threat hunting is a proactive process of searching for evidence of malicious activity that

00:00:04.380 --> 00:00:06.065
may already exist within an environment.

00:00:06.065 --> 00:00:08.000
It is disciplined investigation,

00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:11.120
not guesswork or a dramatic search for clues without evidence.

00:00:11.120 --> 00:00:14.000
Unlike routine alert response, hunts often begin with a hypothesis.

00:00:14.000 --> 00:00:18.060
A hunter may ask whether a suspicious behavior could be occurring quietly,

00:00:18.060 --> 00:00:19.050
whether an account is being misused,

00:00:19.050 --> 00:00:22.085
or whether a technique could leave traces in available telemetry.

00:00:22.085 --> 00:00:25.120
The proactive nature of hunting changes the starting point.

00:00:25.120 --> 00:00:28.130
Instead of waiting for an alert to define the investigation,

00:00:28.130 --> 00:00:31.245
hunters use threat intelligence, environmental knowledge, adversary behavior,

00:00:31.245 --> 00:00:34.050
and prior incidents to form useful questions.

00:00:34.050 --> 00:00:37.935
Threat hunting focuses on uncovering hidden threats through systematic investigation,

00:00:37.935 --> 00:00:40.060
analysis, and evidence gathering.

00:00:40.060 --> 00:00:43.000
The result may be an incident, a detection improvement, a documented gap,

00:00:43.000 --> 00:00:46.000
or stronger confidence in an existing control.
